 "target": 64.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "The 1904 Olympic marathon was won by a man on rat poison.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 4.422
  },
  {
   "text": "It was ninety degrees in St. Louis, on dusty dirt roads.",
   "s": 4.722,
   "e": 8.257
  },
  {
   "text": "Cars drove ahead of the runners, kicking up clouds of dust.",
   "s": 8.557,
   "e": 11.78
  },
  {
   "text": "One runner nearly died from breathing it in.",
   "s": 12.08,
   "e": 14.277
  },
  {
   "text": "And there was just one water stop, at mile twelve.",
   "s": 14.577,
   "e": 17.236
  },
  {
   "text": "Thirty-two men started. Only fourteen would finish.",
   "s": 17.536,
   "e": 20.61
  },
  {
   "text": "Fred Lorz got cramps, so he hopped into a car,",
   "s": 20.91,
   "e": 23.71
  },
  {
   "text": "rode eleven miles, then jumped out and jogged across the finish line in first place.",
   "s": 23.89,
   "e": 28.982
  },
  {
   "text": "He was posing with the president's daughter when officials found out.",
   "s": 29.282,
   "e": 32.569
  },
  {
   "text": "Meanwhile, a Cuban mailman had lost his travel money gambling and hitchhiked to the race.",
   "s": 32.869,
   "e": 38.035
  },
  {
   "text": "He ran in street clothes, stopped to eat rotten apples, and took a nap.",
   "s": 38.335,
   "e": 42.206
  },
  {
   "text": "He still finished fourth.",
   "s": 42.506,
   "e": 43.702
  },
  {
   "text": "Another runner was chased a mile off course by wild dogs. He came ninth.",
   "s": 44.002,
   "e": 48.373
  },
  {
   "text": "And the winner, Thomas Hicks? His trainers fed him strychnine, egg whites and brandy.",
   "s": 48.673,
   "e": 53.198
  },
  {
   "text": "He was hallucinating, and they practically carried him to the finish.",
   "s": 53.498,
   "e": 57.002
  },
  {
   "text": "His time was the slowest winning time in Olympic history.",
   "s": 57.302,
   "e": 60.354
  }
 ],
